  "findings": [
    "Native reverse is inline in both composed consumers; same checkpoint upper_bound retains 10 instructions per iteration with two csel selections.",
    "Exactly one 16-byte selected-group width q load per query, followed by widened two-half prefix additions, low-to-high carry, unsigned comparisons and rank reduction. No decoded geometry, libc calls, vector spill stores, or whole-block preprocessing.",
    "Loaded-group region includes 25 instructions: one q load, one local offset subtraction, then 23 vector/reduction instructions. Rank group-base addition and checkpoint selection are separately charged.",
    "The compiler combines first-stage widening additions into uaddw/uaddw2. Reduction folds high true mask FFFF as subtraction from low true count bit 1, yielding 0/1/2 per lane; addv sums valid endpoints<=offset.",
    "Direct16/direct32 scattered functions both 440 B and same 10-instruction csel binary-search shape; endpoint widths/strides differ. No SIMD, calls or hot spills in those baselines.",
    "Scattered query generation performs a runtime udiv for block=query/cap and another udiv/msub for hashed byte offset, common across formats. Count and terminal extent reads, tomb lookup, output stores and checksum remain charged.",
    "All output arrays are 2048 B. Native scattered/block frames 2112 B; scalar scattered 2128 B due an extra save slot; direct scattered 2112 B. These are save areas plus output, not temporary decoded geometry."
  ]
